# Type narrowing and safety

- Never use a type assertion when control-flow narrowing can solve the problem.
- Narrow values with `if`, `switch`, early `return`, early `throw`, `typeof`, `instanceof`, `in`, and `Array.isArray`.
- Use discriminated unions for stateful data and branch on the discriminant.
- Prefer user-defined type guards when built-in narrowing is not enough.
- Avoid `as` in conditionals and branch bodies unless there is no sound alternative.
- When handling nullable values, narrow first instead of asserting non-null.
- Make switches over tagged unions exhaustive.
